Mark the end of each startup phase, with almost no output

func 0x9ad2b8 resolves to __zone_site_register, and there is no -zt boot argument,
so zone_tagging_on is false and those 644 calls return immediately.  A no-op
function cannot stall, so the thing that stops is most likely the console: the
last few rounds printed six hundred lines or more, and the panel is a 40-line
overwrite buffer driven by the log queue.

Print one marker per phase instead -- after the loop in
kernel_startup_initialize_upto, with the phase number.  Ten lines total, so the
console cannot be the limit, and the last marker says how far the boot really
got.
---
diff --git a/osfmk/kern/startup.c b/osfmk/kern/startup.c
--- a/osfmk/kern/startup.c
+++ b/osfmk/kern/startup.c
@@ -437,3 +437,4 @@ kernel_startup_initialize_upto(startup_subsystem_id_t upto)
 		startup_entry_cur = ++cur;
 	}
+	printf("\nE%u", (unsigned)upto);
 	kernel_startup_log(upto);
